# Backrest on Railway
# Zero template variables: first-run setup (admin username + password)
# happens in the web UI, and repositories/plans are created there too.
# Copy this file to .env only if you run the wrapper outside Railway.

# Injected by Railway automatically — do not set these yourself:
# PORT — mapped by entrypoint.sh to BACKREST_PORT (0.0.0.0:$PORT).
# RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN — the public URL of this deployment.

# Consumed by the wrapper (baked defaults; override only if you know why):
# BACKREST_DATA=/data — all Backrest state on the Railway volume.
# BACKREST_CONFIG=/data/config.json — admin account, repos, plans.
# BACKREST_RESTIC_COMMAND=/bin/restic — restic shipped in the image.

# Upstream Backrest variables that also apply (see README Configuration):
# BACKREST_PORT — overridden by the wrapper from PORT; do not set directly.
# BACKREST_MULTIHOST_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL — e.g. 600s (upstream default).
# TZ — container timezone for schedule evaluation (default UTC).
